romanized_response:
HTTP status code 429 Too Many Requests ante server lo edo oka rakam rate limit undi, mee request danini daatindi ani ardham. Idi kindi karanallo edaina valla jaragochu:

1. Ee request chese code ni chinna time lo chala sarlu run chesaru, anduke rate limit exceed ayindi.

2. Website spam ani anumaninche requests ni 429 status code tho reject chestundi. Dini ardham user agent common browser kaakapovachu, konni websites use chese simple check idi. Dinni rectify cheyadaniki, GET request ki "User-Agent" header ni ila add cheyachu:

```
const response = await axios.get('https://www.realestate.com.au/rent/in-sydney,+nsw/list-1', 
     { headers: { 'User-Agent': 'browser.version' }  }
);
```

Note: meeru `"browser.version"` ni actual browser user agent string tho replace cheyyali. Ee code e application lo run avutundo dani batti, idi user agent spoofing ga consider avvachu. Adi konni countries leda organizations laws prakaram restrict ayi undochu, leda code access cheyadaniki try chestunna website terms of service prakaram kuda restrict ayi undochu.

3. Website inkoka karanam valla requests ki rate limit pedutondi. Request proxy through ga velladam valla idi jaragochu; ala aithe aa proxy ni use chestunna vere users chala ekkuva requests chestu undochu, kani idi unlikely.

4. Website denial of service attack lo undadam valla anni requests ni reject chestondi. Idi unlikely, endukante alanti attack lo unna server typical behavior traffic ni non-existent server ki route cheyadam, leda poorthiga deny cheyadam, valid response emi ivvakapovadam. Ayina, website HTTP status code tho respond chesina kuda, server overload ayinappudu iche 503 Service Unavailable ane server error ravadaniki ekkuva chance undi.

response_en:
Yes, certainly! The issue you're encountering is because the string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", and "buzz" are temporary values, and you are trying to return a reference to them, which is not allowed because they will be dropped at the end of the scope, and the returned reference would be dangling.

You can fix this error by returning &'static str instead of &str. &'static str refers to string literals, which have a 'static lifetime, meaning they last for the duration of the program. Here's an updated version of your code:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Note that the last arm returns a &'static str that is created from a String using the Box::leak function, which takes ownership of a Box<T> and returns a pointer to its contents, effectively leaking it. This is safe because the returned pointer will last for the duration of the program, but it should be used with care as it will not be cleaned up automatically.

romanized_response:
Avunu, tappakunda! Meeru edurkontunna issue endukante string literals "fizzbuzz", "fizz", mariyu "buzz" temporary values, mariyu meeru vaatiki reference return cheyyadaniki try chestunnaru. Adi allowed kaadu, endukante avi scope chivarilo drop aipothayi, mariyu return chesina reference dangling avutundi.

Ee error ni fix cheyyadaniki &str baduluga &'static str return cheyyachu. &'static str ante string literals ni refer chestundi, vaatiki 'static lifetime untundi, ante program duration mottham avi untayi. Mee code yokka updated version ikkada undi:

fn fizzbuzz(n: usize) -> &'static str {
    match (n % 3, n % 5) {
        (0, 0) => "fizzbuzz",
        (0, _) => "fizz",
        (_, 0) => "buzz",
        _ => {
            let s = n.to_string();
            Box::leak(s.into_boxed_str())
        }
    }
}

Gamaninchandi, last arm oka &'static str return chestundi. Adi Box::leak function use chesi String nundi create chestaru. Ee function Box<T> yokka ownership teesukoni, daani contents ki pointer return chestundi, ante practical ga daanni leak chestundi. Return chesina pointer program duration mottham untundi kabatti idi safe, kaani idi automatically clean up avvadu kabatti jagrattaga use cheyyali.

response_en:
Merge sort is a divide and conquer algorithm that works by recursively splitting the input array in half until the arrays are split into single elements. Then, the sorted arrays are merged back together in sorted order.

The key benefits of merge sort over a simpler algorithm like bubble sort are:

1. It is a stable sort that does not change the relative order of elements with equal keys.
2. It has an efficiency of O(n log n) time complexity, making it a relatively efficient algorithm even for large input sizes. Bubble sort, on the other hand, has a quadratic time complexity of O(n^2), making it very inefficient for larger inputs.
3. It is a generic algorithm that can sort any type of data for which a comparison function exists.

Here is a Rust implementation example:
```rust
fn merge_sort(vec: &mut [i32]) {
    if vec.len() < 2 {
        return;
    }

    let mid = vec.len() / 2;
    let (left, right) = vec.split_at_mut(mid);

    merge_sort(left);
    merge_sort(right);

    merge(left, right, vec);
}

fn merge(left: &mut [i32], right: &mut [i32], vec: &mut [i32]) {
    let mut i = 0;
    let mut j = 0;
    let mut k = 0;

    while i < left.len() && j < right.len() {
        if left[i] < right[j] {
            vec[k] = left[i];
            i += 1;
        } else {
            vec[k] = right[j];
            j += 1;
        }
        k += 1;
    }

    while i < left.len() {
        vec[k] = left[i];
        i += 1;
        k += 1;
    }

    while j < right.len() {
        vec[k] = right[j];
        j += 1;
        k += 1;
    }
}
```

romanized_response:
Merge sort anedi divide and conquer algorithm. Idi input array ni recursively half ga split chesthu, arrays single elements ga split ayye varaku pani chestundi. Tarvata, sorted arrays ni sorted order lo malli kalipi merge chestaru.

Bubble sort lanti simple algorithm tho compare cheste, merge sort yokka key benefits ivi:

1. Idi stable sort, ante equal keys unna elements relative order ni marchadu.
2. Deeni efficiency O(n log n) time complexity, kabatti large input sizes ki kuda idi relatively efficient algorithm. Inko vaipu, bubble sort ki O(n^2) ane quadratic time complexity untundi, kabatti large inputs ki chala inefficient.
3. Idi generic algorithm, comparison function unna ye type data ni aina sort cheyyagaladu.

Ikkada oka Rust implementation example undi:
```rust
